course: dictionary
lesson: 8012
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and reel is one of them. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. These are its context, and they give you clues.
explain: «Social media often shows only people's best moments, a "highlight reel", which can make others seem better than they are.» Here a highlight reel is a short video of the best moments, not a spool of thread. The clues are social media and best moments.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If "reeling from the news" meant a fast dance, the sentence would make no sense. It means the person was shocked or confused.
fact: A reel is a round thing that thread, film, fishing line or wire is wound on.
fact: A reel is also a fast, lively folk dance from Scotland or Ireland, and the music for it.
fact: To reel in a fish means to pull it towards you by winding in the line.
fact: To reel means to walk unsteadily, as if about to fall, or to feel shocked or confused.
fact: On social media, a reel is a short video, such as on Instagram.
exercise: Ella says, "My head is reeling." What does reeling mean here? | Walking steadily along the path | *Feeling shocked or confused | Winding a fishing line onto a reel | Dancing a fast Scottish reel
exercise: «Social media often shows only people's best moments, a "highlight reel".» What is a highlight reel? | A lively Irish dance | *A short video of the best moments | A long list said very fast | A round spool of cotton
exercise: At the ceilidh, the band plays a fast Scottish reel. What is a reel here? | To walk unsteadily | *A lively folk dance and its music | A round thing thread is wound on | A short video on an app
test: After the punch, the boxer reeled and nearly fell. What does reeled mean? | Wound a line onto a spool | Danced a fast reel | Watched a short video | *Walked unsteadily, as if about to fall
test: Ben can reel off all the planets in order without stopping. What does reel off mean? | Pull a fish in by winding a line | Feel shocked by the news | Dance in a circle | *Say a long list quickly
exam: In which sentence does reel mean a round thing that thread is wound on? | The news left him reeling | The band played a reel all night | He reeled in a big trout from the loch | *She bought a new cotton reel for her sewing
